Slot 010 is spent, not free.

010_reporting_capture_contract.sql restored the mcp_tool_executions reporting
capture to the versioned contract's column list and stripped the three
off-contract keys from queued outbox facts. It recreated the capture trigger
with EXECUTE FUNCTION sp_capture_reporting_change(), a function that only the
events extension's declarative schema defines -- in the dependent phase, after
every migration has run. On a database that had never booted on a
reporting-era core the function did not exist yet, and the migration failed
every upgrade at "function sp_capture_reporting_change() does not exist".

The view and trigger are declarative state (schema/reporting_capture.sql) and
need no migration; the outbox repair moved to 013_reporting_fact_repair.sql,
guarded so it runs only where the facts can exist. Deployments that applied
010 keep their tracking row; 013 is a no-op for them.

Numbering continues at the highest slot ever used, never at the first gap.
